  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef had collected NNN notes of Rs. 200020002000 to pay his total college fees. However, the government banned Rs. 200020002000 notes.\n\nChef wants to pay the same amount using Rs. 500500500 notes only. Find the number of notes Chef needs.\n\n\nInput Format\nEach test case consists of a single integer NNN - the number of notes of Rs. 200020002000 that Chef has collected.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput a single integer - the number of Rs. 500500500 notes needed.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4",
        "output": "16",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\n444 notes of Rs. 200020002000 make a total of 4⋅2000=80004 \\cdot 2000 = 80004⋅2000=8000 rupees. This is equivalent to 161616 notes of  Rs. 500500500."
      }
    ]
  },
